# check_coverage.py allow-list -- intentional coverage gaps only.
# Format: <os> <tag|*> <workflow>   # reason
# Every line below is backed by real evidence (a workflow comment, the
# builder's releases.json sync field, table.md/README, or git history);
# the evidence is cited in the comment block above each entry. Genuine
# coverage holes are NOT listed here; they stay failing and get reported.

# blissos (Android guest): scp is the only sync backend -- blissos.yml's
# own comment says "no rsync/sshfs/nfs on Android" (VM_SYNC_METHODS=scp in
# blissos-builder/releases.json). blissos.yml already exercises scp
# directly on ubuntu-24.04, windows-latest AND macos-latest, so the
# shared cross-host jobs below would be pure duplication.
blissos * test.yml
blissos * testmacos.yml
blissos * testwindows.yml

# dragonflybsd: testsync exercises sshfs+scp+rsync together. dragonflybsd-
# builder's table.md documents "sshfs is not offered on DragonFlyBSD --
# the sshfs (FUSE) mount is read-only in practice ... so only rsync/scp/nfs
# are listed" (releases.json sync=rsync,scp,nfs, no sshfs). dragonflybsd
# stays in testnfs/testsysnfs (nfs-only), only testsync is affected.
dragonflybsd * test.yml

# nextbsd: test.yml's own comment above the testnfs job says it plainly --
# "nextbsd is in this job (the bundled user-space nfsd) but deliberately
# NOT in testsysnfs below: only the user-space path has been verified on
# it." nextbsd is already present in testsync/testnfs; only testsysnfs is
# affected.
nextbsd * test.yml

# omnios: omnios.yml's own comment -- "OmniOS has no FUSE sshfs
# (VM_SSHFS_PKG is empty), so sshfs is not offered" (releases.json
# sync=rsync,scp,nfs for every release). omnios stays in testnfs/
# testsysnfs; only testsync (which needs sshfs) is affected.
omnios * test.yml

# openindiana: testsync tests exactly sshfs+scp+rsync. openindiana's own
# dedicated openindiana.yml ALREADY runs that same trio (plus nfs) directly
# for every release (matrix sync: [sshfs, scp, nfs, rsync]), so duplicating
# it in the shared testsync job adds no coverage. openindiana stays in
# testnfs/testsysnfs.
openindiana * test.yml

# plan9 (9front): has no sshd, so it cannot reuse the ssh-based
# testrun.yml that testsync/testnfs/testsysnfs (and the macos/windows
# jobs) all route through -- test.yml/testmacos.yml/testwindows.yml each
# say so directly in the comment above their own dedicated "plan9" job,
# which already verifies boot + telnet-exec + 9P-sync (Linux) or telnet-
# exec (macOS/Windows) on that same workflow file.
plan9 * test.yml
plan9 * testmacos.yml
plan9 * testwindows.yml

# solaris: solaris.yml's own comment -- "Solaris has no FUSE sshfs
# (VM_SSHFS_PKG is unset), so sshfs is omitted" (releases.json
# sync=rsync,scp,nfs). solaris stays in testnfs/testsysnfs; only testsync
# (which needs sshfs) is affected.
solaris * test.yml

# tribblix: releases.json sync=rsync,scp,nfs for every release (no sshfs),
# and tribblix.yml's own matrix never tests sshfs either. tribblix stays
# in testnfs/testsysnfs; only testsync is affected.
tribblix * test.yml

# The -build variants (base OS plus a preinstalled build-essential
# toolchain) are deliberately untested -- maintainer decision 2026-07-26:
# the base release of each already exercises the same boot/sync paths.
omnios r151054-build omnios.yml
omnios r151056-build omnios.yml
omnios r151058-build omnios.yml
openindiana 202510-build openindiana.yml
openindiana 202604-build openindiana.yml

# The solaris toolchain variants (base 11.4 plus a specific newer
# compiler toolchain) are deliberately untested -- maintainer decision
# 2026-07-26: 11.4 and 11.4-gcc already exercise the same boot/sync paths.
solaris 11.4-gcc-14 solaris.yml
solaris 11.4-clang-19 solaris.yml
